WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:17.331
I've said, Jerry Barker believed in having Sundays off.

2
00:00:18.392 --> 00:00:22.055
Spending time with his family was worth more to him than any money he might earn.

3
00:00:23.717 --> 00:00:27.560
One day he was hitching me to the cab when a gentleman walked into the stable yard.

4
00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:29.541
I recognized the man.

5
00:00:30.502 --> 00:00:32.564
We often carried him and his wife around town.

6
00:00:35.628 --> 00:00:36.369
"Good morning, Mr.

7
00:00:36.409 --> 00:00:38.110
Briggs," Jerry said politely.

8
00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:41.453
"Good morning," the gentleman replied.

9
00:00:41.473 --> 00:00:44.636
"I came to offer you a business arrangement.

10
00:00:46.077 --> 00:00:50.881
Mrs. Briggs and I have decided to try a new church, and it's too far to walk.

11
00:00:51.982 --> 00:00:54.825
We'd like to have you drive us there each Sunday morning."

12
00:00:54.845 --> 00:00:57.507
"Thank you, sir," Jerry said.

13
00:00:57.527 --> 00:00:59.129
"But I'm afraid I can't.

14
00:00:59.529 --> 00:01:00.710
I never work on Sundays."

15
00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:06.293
"I understand, but of course we'd pay extra for your trouble," Mr.

16
00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:06.874
Briggs said.

17
00:01:06.894 --> 00:01:09.255
"It would only be a short trip."

18
00:01:10.715 --> 00:01:11.655
Jerry shook his head.

19
00:01:11.675 --> 00:01:14.076
"I'm sorry, sir.

20
00:01:14.777 --> 00:01:17.438
I used to work seven days a week, and it was miserable.

21
00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:22.080
Year in and year out, never a day's rest for me or the horses.

22
00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:25.941
I didn't get to spend any time with my wife and children.

23
00:01:27.022 --> 00:01:31.423
For the past five years I've made it a rule not to work on Sundays, and we're all

24
00:01:31.483 --> 00:01:32.764
happier than we've ever been."

25
00:01:34.576 --> 00:01:35.117
"I see."

26
00:01:35.537 --> 00:01:36.618
Mr. Briggs frowned.

27
00:01:36.638 --> 00:01:39.560
"I suppose I'll have to find another cab."

28
00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.603
He walked away, and Jerry gave me a pat.

29
00:01:44.764 --> 00:01:47.326
"I'm afraid I've disappointed him, Jack," he said.

30
00:01:47.346 --> 00:01:49.867
"But we can't give up our Sundays."

31
00:01:51.849 --> 00:01:54.751
When Polly came outside, he told her what had happened.

32
00:01:54.771 --> 00:01:58.674
"It was difficult to say no," Jerry said.

33
00:01:58.694 --> 00:02:01.616
"Mrs. Briggs is one of my best customers.

34
00:02:02.676 --> 00:02:08.059
She often goes shopping or visiting for hours at a time, and always pays the whole fare without

35
00:02:08.179 --> 00:02:13.782
arguing. She's never in a hurry, and driving her around is easy work for the horses.

36
00:02:14.883 --> 00:02:17.064
We might lose her as a customer because of this.

37
00:02:17.564 --> 00:02:18.565
What do you think, Polly?"

38
00:02:19.785 --> 00:02:22.507
"I think you did the right thing," Polly said.

39
00:02:22.527 --> 00:02:26.129
"I remember how things were when you worked all the time.

40
00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:31.512
I wouldn't go back to those days even if you earned twice what you do now!"

41
00:02:33.676 --> 00:02:36.578
For three weeks after that, we saw no sign of Mrs.

42
00:02:36.638 --> 00:02:40.961
Briggs. I could tell Jerry missed both her company and her fares.

43
00:02:43.623 --> 00:02:47.806
One evening Polly announced that a servant had come that day to ask Jerry to pick up Mrs.

44
00:02:47.866 --> 00:02:48.827
Briggs the next morning.

45
00:02:48.847 --> 00:02:52.149
"I said you would, of course," Polly said.

46
00:02:52.169 --> 00:02:56.232
"But I also said I was surprised, since we thought Mrs.

47
00:02:56.332 --> 00:02:57.833
Briggs had hired someone else."

48
00:02:57.853 --> 00:03:00.615
"What did the servant say?"

49
00:03:00.935 --> 00:03:01.596
Jerry asked.

50
00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:03.441
"He said Mr.

51
00:03:03.461 --> 00:03:08.905
Briggs was annoyed that you wouldn't work on Sundays, so he'd been trying other cabs," Polly reported.

52
00:03:08.925 --> 00:03:10.486
"But Mrs.

53
00:03:10.566 --> 00:03:12.267
Briggs wasn't happy with any of them.

54
00:03:13.928 --> 00:03:18.451
Some drove too fast, some too slow, and none were as nice and clean as yours.

55
00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:21.494
So she insisted they hire you again!"

56
00:03:22.775 --> 00:03:25.076
Jerry was glad to have his favorite customer back.

57
00:03:26.217 --> 00:03:29.940
He was just as glad he'd stood by his decision not to work on Sundays.

58
00:03:31.084 --> 00:03:35.025
But one day soon after that, he made an exception to his Sunday rule.

59
00:03:36.986 --> 00:03:41.247
A neighbor needed a ride out into the country to visit her dying mother, and he agreed to

60
00:03:41.307 --> 00:03:41.667
take her.

61
00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:46.749
"It's the right thing to do," Polly agreed when he told her.

62
00:03:47.409 --> 00:03:49.209
"Poor Dinah has no other option.

63
00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:53.111
And we should always try to treat others as we'd like to be treated.

64
00:03:54.251 --> 00:03:57.752
I would certainly appreciate a ride to visit my own mother if I needed it."

65
00:03:59.408 --> 00:04:01.470
I was chosen for the journey, and we set out.

66
00:04:04.552 --> 00:04:08.595
I was tired from the work week, but Jerry had borrowed a lighter cart for the trip.

67
00:04:09.836 --> 00:04:12.738
After the heavy four-wheeled cab, it felt easy to pull.

68
00:04:14.179 --> 00:04:18.102
It was a fine May day, and it was nice to leave the city behind and breathe the

69
00:04:18.162 --> 00:04:19.102
fresh country air.

70
00:04:20.723 --> 00:04:22.805
Dinah's family lived in a small farmhouse.

71
00:04:23.806 --> 00:04:26.788
Two cows were grazing peacefully in the grassy field behind it.

72
00:04:28.628 --> 00:04:32.449
"You can tie your horse in the cowshed while you wait," a young man said.

73
00:04:32.469 --> 00:04:35.710
"I wish we had a better stable to offer you."

74
00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:42.252
"If your cows wouldn't mind, I'm sure there's nothing my horse would like better than an hour or

75
00:04:42.292 --> 00:04:44.493
two out in the grass," Jerry said.

76
00:04:45.693 --> 00:04:47.133
The young man agreed gladly.

77
00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:51.875
Jerry led me into the field, removed my harness, and set me free.

78
00:04:53.915 --> 00:04:55.776
I could hardly believe my good fortune!

79
00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.001
At first I wasn't sure what to do.

80
00:05:00.142 --> 00:05:01.022
Should I graze?

81
00:05:02.163 --> 00:05:03.404
Roll in the soft grass?

82
00:05:03.944 --> 00:05:06.205
Lie down to rest?

83
00:05:06.225 --> 00:05:08.367
Or gallop across the field out of sheer freedom?

84
00:05:09.647 --> 00:05:10.748
I did all those things.

85
00:05:12.589 --> 00:05:17.372
Jerry smiled as he watched me, and I knew he was glad we had come—even on a Sunday.
